{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794823490,"nonce":"27+7U/BTzeSX3Dig3wtO/v2lNXI=","message":"Capabilities, decided 2026-11-16: wgpu-style features and limits rather than a lowest common denominator. The API covers everything any backend can do. Each device reports its features, such as compute and storage buffers, and its limits, such as maximum texture size and buffer binding size. A program names the features it requires when it opens a device, and backends without them are skipped. Using a feature the device lacks throws an error naming the feature and the backend, so no part of the API is dropped because one driver cannot do it.\n\nhaxelib check: with -lib hxn-gpu (hxn 0.3.4) and -lib hxn-gpu-metal 0.1.0 (hxn 0.3.2), haxelib path resolves hxn to 0.3.4 alone, without an error. Whether a 0.1.0 native driver's library works with hxn 0.3.4's classes is checked when its backend first runs.","files":null}]}